tegory term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac319428a892326a24fe01033ef0e2953cf4fda1f74391567caad1f287adfbaf</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>37 years after fall of Berlin Wall: How divided are Germans?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf45f7afab90ccd470ea65b656e6f14f1b773caa16359f36c72ef96e3e015b17</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/37-years-after-fall-of-berlin-wall-how-divided-are-germans/a-79877461--471b79fce1fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/37-years-after-fall-of-berlin-wall-how-divided-are-germans/a-79877461?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three artists share their thoughts on the reunification of East and West Germany. How do they perceive a shared "we" and what gives them cause for optimism?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Potter films turns 25 ahead of new TV series' release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2a28e46ef077a74a2f8358ef744babfe5f66970c08f9c8add69c1b5a8149cb7</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-potter-films-turns-25-ahead-of-new-tv-series-release/a-79856130--db1dcb8d550c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-potter-films-turns-25-ahead-of-new-tv-series-release/a-79856130?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 2001, "Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone" hit cinemas and took the world by storm. Today, anticipation for the new series is high, but its creator, J.K. Rowling, remains a controversial figure.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's celebrated children's author Janosch has died</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:851f40fa533dbae624b4d74030291303fbd260df8cd22553254c9ffe0c1a06f5</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600--a3fdc8a2501b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bear, Tiger and Tiger-Duck: The author and illustrator Janosch achieved world fame with his heartwarming children's figures. He died at the age of 95.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian activist and Nobel Peace Prize winner Narges Mohammadi shares her story in memoir</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ce3ddc73283014ab4341e552379234c526da7b5c3c57f85ebc17dafe18b8ecd</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167--a983bd7e2dcc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-activist-and-nobel-peace-prize-winner-narges-mohammadi-shares-her-story-in-memoir/a-79868167?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Written and smuggled out of prison, the 2023 Nobel Prize laureate's memoir reveals the cost of defying Iran's regime and fighting for freedom.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>'Never Again!': Holocaust remembrance under pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dab1ff746c1b38a606cc98487fd36a99e35fb81a8a3ba99ee9203e650c712650</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/never-again-holocaust-remembrance-under-pressure/a-79840894--861f4756e8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/never-again-holocaust-remembrance-under-pressure/a-79840894?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Only a few Holocaust survivors remain who can share their stories firsthand. Meanwhile, voices calling for an end to what they describe as a "cult of guilt" are growing louder. How can Holocaust remembrance survive?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Berlin's Arab queers are building their community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20cb7b2c76d96c0828e2e1f315525f940ebf1521f71b37e47f56fe0e6f59f582</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143--c676c7f349f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the co-founder of the ADIRA Drag Festival, Lebanese performance artist, drag performer, DJ and cultural organizer Hassandra has become an essential part of Berlin's queer artistic landscape.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey impasse as Russia threatens sanctions on Canada, Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ea869e25d2b8faa463330492a1fa5fc4bd8a7ad5ef2a01b6dbaaa1a261b8899</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676--52aad908ad79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two weeks after the CAS ordered ice hockey's governing body to reintegrate Russia into international play, a solution remains elusive. Now Russia has threatened to take legal action against two tournament hosts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why malnutrition can go unnoticed, and what that means for our health</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f5f33f62321cd1c01e9f85a134aa784b03938f9a6024894baefb6b69d8ec56b</id><updated>2026-11-16T06:50:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-malnutrition-can-go-unnoticed-and-what-that-means-for-our-health/a-79871016--a7247c0af1e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-malnutrition-can-go-unnoticed-and-what-that-means-for-our-health/a-79871016?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 2 billion people worldwide suffer from nutrient deficiencies, most of them in the Global South. The health consequences can be devastating.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry></feed>
